 "$comment": "AEP-0002 Annex A machine-usable mapping fixture for the Cline table (the SUBPROCESS hook generation — ten zod-typed events, verified against the published @cline/shared@0.0.59 dist/hooks/events.d.ts; the extension protobuf generation is out of scope by the design record). Each entry pins the pure hook->events mapping at the adapter default posture (capture metadata): input is one typed stdin payload; expected is an ARRAY of {type, data, subject?, step?} — agent terminals with a typed parent id also close the delegation pair, and the per-turn iteration counter stamps the envelope step (no run.step.* synthesis: the surface exposes no boundary moments). Envelope identity (taskId -> session; REAL run boundaries with adapter-minted run ids; tool pairing by the typed call id) is runtime state, pinned by the reference adapter smoke. OBSERVE-ONLY: nothing maps to attention.* (approvals ride the hub channel, deferred by recorded decision) and hook responses never carry the agent-mutating control fields.",
 "identity": {
  "session_from": "taskId",
  "run_from": null,
  "$comment": "No run id is exposed; boundaries are REAL (agent_start/agent_resume open, agent_end/agent_abort/agent_error close) and the adapter mints the id. iteration -> envelope step as a plain string."
 },
